        "schema" : "http://google.com/profiles/media/provider",
        "term" : "youtube"
      } ],
      "content" : "Read all about this project at my website: http://www.andybrown.me.uk\n\nThis video gives you a quick tour of my open source FPGA graphics accelerator board followed by a walkthrough of the graphics accelerator powering a theoretical platform game.\n\nThe controller MCU on the board is an STM32F429VIT6. The FPGA is a Xilinx Spartan 3 XC3S50 and the LCD is a 640x360 panel taken from a Sony Ericsson Vivaz U5 cellphone and reverse engineered by myself (see website for that reverse engineering project and free software)\n\nVisit my website to see the full writeup, get the hardware design files and all the VHDL and C++ firmware code. It's all free, come and get it!",
